"notes": "Modified cash basis village (basis cash). Governmental = Total Governmental Funds column p4; beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balance (cash basis; includes certificates of deposit, restricted cash, county treasurer cash, so investments not shown separately). The Taxes line 667,830 (p4) is split using the general receipts on p2 (property 466,496, sales and use 146,048, motor vehicle 46,980, occupation 1,000, special assessment 7,306; sum 667,830). Governmental roll-forward: 1,480,516 + 1,152,122 - 1,195,001 + 196,556 - 244,272 = 1,389,921. Business-type = Water and Sewer, Total column p6, measure cash (modified cash net position); operating transfer in 47,716; roll-forward 442,445 + 237,003 - 438,146 + 47,716 = 289,018. Business-type receipts/disbursements have no single printed total, so computed. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis, Total column (p1); no liabilities. Detail: the p7 budgetary comparison schedule gives only fund-level actual totals (no lines; budget only as grand total 1,464,188 receipts / 2,633,450 disbursements) so it is not itemized into detail; Library 7,138 and Park 9,240 receipts there are inside Other Governmental on p4. Because no line-level budget schedule exists, per-fund Water and Sewer operating lines come from the p6 business-type statement and cover operating receipts and operating disbursements; the p6 nonoperating lines (interest income, loan payments, capital projects) are recorded per fund under a separate 'nonoperating' schedule name with no detail_totals, since the statement prints only a net nonoperating total (Water -282,775, Sewer -28,138; the lines tie to it). Transfer cross-check: interfund in 196,556 (General 25,000 from Keno; Street 44,935; Cemetery 13,116; Fire 2,509; Other Governmental 110,996) vs out 244,272 (General 161,479; Debt Service 57,793; Keno 25,000); net 47,716 equals the Water fund operating transfer in on p6 and the internal transfers on p2. All matched; no hidden transfers in spending lines. Statement p4 total column is as printed. Read pages 1-7 of 7",
